====================================================================================================================
DE03 -- the dSph elongation prediction table (directional-EFE programme)
====================================================================================================================
  KILL CONDITIONS (written before any measurement):
    K1 measured dSph elongation ALIGNED WITH THE GALACTIC-CENTRE DIRECTION at the AQUAL-predicted level,
       eps_iso >= the DE03 table's lower edge at that dSph's eta (both footings), no orbital explanation
       -> direction-yes: the framework's direction-blind rule is FALSIFIED in this lane.
    K2 field-aligned elongations consistent with zero (tidal/orbit-aligned only) -> direction-blind SURVIVES.
    K3 anything else, or the two a0 footings disagree -> UNDECIDED.
  MUTATE = 0 (1 breaks the registered-mu2 standardization hinge)

====================================================================================================================
PHASE 1 -- the identity: eps_Phi = (sqrt(1+L) - 1)/(sqrt(1+L) + 1)
====================================================================================================================
  Phi = -GM/(mu r sqrt(1 + L sin^2 t));  r(t)|_Phi = Gm*Ms/(P*mus*sqrt(L*sin(t)**2 + 1))
  r_par = r(0) = Gm*Ms/(P*mus) ;  r_perp = r(pi/2) = Gm*Ms/(P*mus*sqrt(L + 1))
  (r_par - r_perp)/(r_par + r_perp) simplifies to:  (L - sqrt(L + 1) + 1)/(L + sqrt(L + 1) + 1)
  [PASS] C1 identity certified symbolically: (r_par - r_perp)/(r_par + r_perp) == (sqrt(1+L)-1)/(sqrt(1+L)+1)   (derived closed form (L - sqrt(L + 1) + 1)/(L + sqrt(L + 1) + 1); numeric |residual| < 1e-14 over L samples (max 0.0e+00); r_sol solves the fixed-Phi equation: True)

====================================================================================================================
PHASE 2 -- eps_Phi(eta) on the classical range, kernels mu1, mu2_reg (HEADLINE = mu2_reg), mu2_std (reference)
====================================================================================================================
  L(eta) = eta*mu'(eta)/mu(eta):  L_mu1 = 1/(1+eta);  L_mu2reg = 2/((1+eta)(2+eta));  L_mu2std = 1/(1+eta^2)
  2a0-scale footnote (SW01 argument convention u = eta/2, mu2_reg): L = 2/((1+eta/2)(2+eta/2)) -- 0.711 at eta = 0.5 vs 0.533 headlined
  eps_Phi is footing-independent (a function of eta alone); the a0 footings enter through the per-dSph eta (phase 3).
